Report why xz decoding failed instead of always "corrupted data".
Every decoder error, including valid files that use an unsupported
filter (such as a BCJ or delta filter) or a dictionary larger than the
64 MiB limit, and input that is not xz at all, was reported as
"corrupted data", suggesting that the file was damaged. Print "invalid
magic", "unsupported options", "dictionary too large" or "out of memory"
for the corresponding xz_dec_run() results.

---
 archival/libarchive/decompress_unxz.c |   11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/archival/libarchive/decompress_unxz.c
+++ b/archival/libarchive/decompress_unxz.c
@@ -143,7 +143,16 @@
 			continue;
 		}
 		if (xz_result != XZ_OK && xz_result != XZ_UNSUPPORTED_CHECK) {
-			bb_simple_error_msg("corrupted data");
+			const char *msg = "corrupted data";
+			if (xz_result == XZ_MEM_ERROR)
+				msg = bb_msg_memory_exhausted;
+			if (xz_result == XZ_MEMLIMIT_ERROR)
+				msg = "dictionary too large";
+			if (xz_result == XZ_FORMAT_ERROR)
+				msg = "invalid magic";
+			if (xz_result == XZ_OPTIONS_ERROR)
+				msg = "unsupported options";
+			bb_simple_error_msg(msg);
 			total = -1;
 			break;
 		}
